From d23b0cb316721a6529cdd8ebbd8e597cc6094a5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Logan <Logan@cattn.dev>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 12:16:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 12/19] PresentX: device-side WaitFrameEventX and the frame
 pacer share one token source

Device slot 80 (WaitFrameEventX, from #6935) numbered its tokens with a
counter of its own, while XboxPresentation's pacer refuses any token above
the ones it issued itself. A title that waits through the device and
presents through the device's XboxPresentation therefore had every
PresentX refused with E_INVALIDARG once its tokens ran ahead of the
pacer's.

leonida::FrameTokenSource is now the counter both use: a pacer takes an
optional shared source (a standalone pacer still owns its own and numbers
as before), the device proxy owns one and exposes it through
rt::d3d12_xs::device_frame_tokens, and XboxPresentation passes a given
source to its pacer. A token that was never issued is still refused.

Reported by rafaelpssz in #7496.
